# Story: someone who works from the keyboard always sees which window will
# take what they type. The ring is around the focused window, goes where
# commands and clicks send the keyboard, moves with the layout, and is gone when
# the window is out of sight.
# Reference: A15 (docs/features/F37-focus-ring.md).
# The ring is an option: Arbor ships without it (collab/QUESTIONS.md, Q29).
set focusRing true
open Safari
open Notes
open Calculator 300x400
# Nothing is docked yet, so Arbor has not been asked for anything: no ring.
expect ring none
dock 101 left
expect ring 101
dock 102 right
expect ring 102
focus 101
expect ring 101
# It moves with the window.
resize 101 right 120
expect ring 101
zoom 101
expect fills 101
expect ring 101
back
expect ring 101
# A floating window has one too.
focus 103
expect ring 103
move 103 620 300 300 400
expect ring 103
# Out of sight, no ring.
minimize 103
expect ring none
restore 103
expect ring 103
close 103
expect ring none
focus 102
expect ring 102
# Dragged to the other side, it has its ring again when the mouse lets go.
drag 102 3 400 cmd
expect docked 102
expect ring 102
# Back to a normal Mac: the ring goes with the arrangement.
float-all
expect ring none
